<div class="workflow">
  <details open>
    <summary>
      <span class="flow-number">1</span>Establish identity
    </summary>
    <p>
      The operator supplies a profile, an expected AWS account, and selected
      regions. An STS identity check runs before operational reads, helping
      catch work in the wrong environment.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>
      <span class="flow-number">2</span>Investigate the deployment
    </summary>
    <p>
      Collect Amplify Hosting inventory and deployment evidence within the
      selected scope. Contextual errors and meaningful exit codes make partial
      reads visible.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>
      <span class="flow-number">3</span>Compare configuration
    </summary>
    <p>
      Report configuration differences while withholding the underlying values.
      The operator can identify a mismatch without casually exposing
      configuration in the report.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>
      <span class="flow-number">4</span>Review a retry, if needed
    </summary>
    <p>
      The deployment command submits an explicitly reviewed retry. This
      transition is separate from the read-only operational commands and is
      optional.
    </p>
  </details>
</div>
